  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 1201.01 Purpose",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 1201.01 Purpose. The purpose of the rules in this chapter is to:\n\n(a) Prescribe the requirements and limitations for siting, designing, constructing, operating, and closing a facility under the provisions of a permit-by-notification issued pursuant to Env-Sw 311; and\n\n(b) Ensure, through the prescribed requirements and limitations, that permit-by-notification facilities shall be sited, designed, operated, and closed in a manner that does not endanger the public health or adversely affect the environment and which minimizes the potential for accidents that could lead to personal injury or property damage.\n\nSource. #6619-B, eff 10-29-97; (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Sw 1200) ss by #8459, eff 10-28-05 (formerly Env-Wm 2901.01); ss by #10595, eff 7-1-14; ss by #13865, eff 2-6-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw1200.html"
